is as a  success or make meaningless distinctions  like it was a strategic failure but a  logistical success if this is what  success looks like what the heck does  failure look like this has been a fiasco  from start to finish you know part of  the thing that i'm talking about this  week is about the degradation of faith  in american institutions institutions  that used to unite us in feeling proud  of what we offer as a country uh proud  of what we represent to the world and i  think of no institution where this can  prove more damaging than the u.s  military why is it that the military has  become something that where we used to  be able to you know trust it have faith  in it believe that it was going to be  able to execute what needed to be  executed and win wars to one that now  seems to be just another political  football  well i think when it comes to the rank  and file those young marines soldiers  sailors and airmen who are usually at  the tip of the spear we actually have  incredible people in our military doing  a difficult and dangerous job on our  behalf i think the problem is in our  general and flag officer class because  we tend to promote  politicians and not war fighters and  that's a huge problem with a broken  personnel management system in dod as  well as the fact that some of our elite  quote unquote elite war colleges aren't  actually teaching warfighting or the  history of warfighting they've just  become sort of civilianized masters  degree granting programs so we have a  massive problem with how we groom  those officers who show the most  potential to end up being four-star  generals one day and then you have  increasing politicization of those  people wearing stars on their shoulders  it's a huge problem and recent polling  coming out confirms that americans who  used to have you know overwhelming faith  in the military starting to view it as  more of a politicized institution  quickly congressman what can we do to  get rid of this dead weight to get rid  of this problem i mean we can talk about  it brac for generals but how else are we  going to get rid of some of these folks  with stars on on on their uniforms who  really are it seems like not serving the  institution well  well a few things i i mentioned the war  college problem i do think we need to  completely reform our entire war college  and so only the best of the best get to  go and they actually practice how do you  deter china from invading a taiwan in  the most stressing national security  scenarios the second is it really is  actually bigger than any one personality  who's controversial like general milly  it's this entire diversity equity and  inclusion bureaucracy that is being  built within the pentagon and we are  going to have to when we take back the  house go through all of that and  dismantle it because it's actually  harmful to unit cohesion the military  has to be a pure meritocracy and if you  start to view everything through the  prism of race you're going to start to  really screw up our ability to fight and  win wars and that's the final thing our  north star when it comes to the military  has to be the ability to fight and win  wars that's what it's all about  absolutely congressman  very important work thanks so much for  joining me tonight  thank you hey sean hannity here hey  click here to subscribe to fox news  youtube page and catch our hottest  interviews and most compelling analysis  you will not get it anywhere else
 

